    "name": "night-owl",
    "note": "Night Owl (VS Code sdras.night-owl 2.1.1): dark is 'Night Owl', light is 'Night Owl Light' (Light Owl). Dark keeps the deep #011627; light's surface is its UI chrome #F0F0F0 (the editor's #FBFBFB leaves the bevel no room above it). The accent is Night Owl's blue, the colour both variants use most; the terminal is the VS Code themes' integrated palette. Light Owl has no orange: warn is the mix of its red and its yellow. Departures: Light Owl's bright green (color10) is #4D9A2B (its green and cyan were too close for the power reel) and its faint text #8496A0 (2.7:1); Night Owl's muted text is a greyer #9AA3AD than the sidebar's #89A4BB, which sat beside its blue. Group tabs: the tab is the orange, a locked group's tab the teal. btop: the stock night-owl in dark, custom in light.",
